fact WorkItem(id: "WI-602", description: some(value: "requires-soundness: a DEFINITE (ground-refuted) value-precondition violation in a RULE BODY is silently accepted. WI-557 scoped the WI-539 call-site precondition check to op-body context (typing.rs check_apply_iter, gate 'if !env.in_rule_body()') to avoid spurious UnsatisfiedPrecondition over SYMBOLIC rule-body vars (which legitimately FLOAT). But the skip is UNCONDITIONAL, so it also swallows a DEFINITE violation: ?b.guarded(0) with a literal 0 -> neq(0,0) is ground-FALSE (refuted, not floating), yet the rule body loads clean while the SAME call in an op body raises 'unsatisfied precondition'. Eval does not re-check value-preconditions either, so a [simp] rule whose RHS is such a call injects the violating term at firing time entirely unchecked. FIX: make the rule-body gate refutation-aware -- in a rule body still RAISE on a ground-REFUTED precondition, skip ONLY a float (the WI-067/WI-292 polarity: act on a DECIDED obligation, never on an UNDETERMINED one); precondition_proved already has the Gamma/ground-eval machinery to distinguish. Regression test (currently #[ignore]d -- fails on the gap, passes once fixed): rule_body_definite_precondition_violation_is_rejected in anthill-core/tests/include/wi557_rule_body_precondition_scope_test.rs; must keep rule_body_value_precondition_dot_dispatches (symbolic float) green. Discovered in the WI-595 dialogue ('op with requires in the right part of simp')."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-603"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-03T06:17:34Z"))
